---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../components/v2/templates/CategoryHub.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../data/images';
import { getPageSEO } from '../utils/seo';

const pageSEO = getPageSEO('grocery');
---

<BaseLayout pageId="grocery" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: pageSEO.h1 }]}>
  <CategoryHub
    title={pageSEO.h1}
    kicker="Ingredient planning"
    intro="Use the Grocery Hub to find conservative information about ingredient sourcing, management, and connected cooking pages."
    relatedLinks={[
      { label: 'Ingredients', href: '/ingredients/' },
      { label: 'Recipes', href: '/recipes/' },
      { label: 'Food', href: '/food/' },
      { label: 'Cooking and Serving Guide', href: '/guides/cooking-and-serving/' },
    ]}
    tableOfContents
    heroImage={siteImages.ingredientsHero}
  >
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>Grocery is the Wiki section for questions about sourcing and managing ingredients. The Ingredients directory identifies the materials currently covered, while the Recipes and Food hubs explain their separate roles in preparation and service.</p>

  <h2 id="how-grocery-connects">How Grocery Connects to Cooking</h2>
  <p>The Wiki organizes these topics as <strong>Grocery → Ingredients → Recipes → Food → Orders</strong>. This is a navigation relationship, not a claim about a fixed shop route, stock guarantee, or refresh schedule. Start here for sourcing questions, then move to the Ingredients directory for an individual item or the Recipe Hub for preparation context.</p>

  <h2 id="ingredient-navigation">Ingredient Navigation</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/ingredients/">Ingredients directory</a> is the main database for Rice, Eggs, Vegetables, Bangus, Pork, Beef, and Condiments. Each entry links back to the broader cooking sections so players can move between ingredient information and restaurant tasks without losing context.</p>

  <h2 id="resource-management">Ingredient Management</h2>
  <p>Use the current game interface to judge what is available and what the restaurant needs. The Wiki does not publish a universal restock schedule, shop refresh interval, sourcing route, or availability promise.</p>
  <p>Keep sourcing questions on this page, item-specific information in the Ingredient Directory, and task steps in the Cooking and Serving Guide.</p>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Check the current restaurant task before deciding which ingredient information to open.</li>
    <li>Use the Ingredients directory when a material name is unfamiliar.</li>
    <li>Use the Recipes guide for workflow help instead of treating Grocery as a recipe list.</li>
    <li>Keep cooking, serving, and ingredient planning connected during busy restaurant sessions.</li>
  </ul>
  </CategoryHub>
</BaseLayout>
